Z||000000||Ricky||05-02-99||10:14 PM||||What is it worth?  103K miles and looks very good. I've owned a 84 2m4 with a natsy habit of melting starter wires.  What should I look for?  They want 3K$.  
Z||000001||VISCERAL||05-03-99||07:36 AM||||Just bought an 87 gt for 2500. It's perfect, 85,ooo miles. I've started replacing stuff, like polyurathanes all around and i'm gonna throw in a new centerforce dual friction clutch and k&n filter this weekend.<br>I'm gonna try to fabricate a better air inlet so I can just have a conical air filter.When I will have the motor out i'll also replace the cradle bushings with poly and wrap the exhaust in thermotec wrap to cool off the bay and also a 160 thermostat and a 176 temp fan switch. Can't ever be too cool with mid engines. Gonna run some redline water wetter in the coolant. I'd also run synthetic oil if i were you. Don't forget to change your fuel filter and use some injector cleaner. good luck
Z||000002||Ricky||05-03-99||10:04 PM||||Thanks for the reply.  Any information on specs? 0 to 60, 1/4 mile speed and time for the v6.  Any information on aftermarket exhaust? Thanks. Ricky
